{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788254521930,"sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-812da8e66f6c050e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, sys\ncsv.field_size_limit(10**9)\n\ndef peek(path, n=5):\n    print(f\"=== {path} ===\")\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        r = csv.reader(f)\n        header = next(r)\n        rows = []\n        for i, row in enumerate(r):\n            if i >= n: break\n            rows.append(row)\n    print(\"cols:\", header)\n    for row in rows: print(row)\n    print()\n\npeek('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\npeek('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96"},"output":"=== data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv ===\ncols: ['round', 'datetime', 'home_team', 'away_team', 'home_goal', 'away_goal', 'season']\n['1', '2012-03-07 16:00:00', 'Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ', 'América - MG', '0', '0', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-14 20:30:00', 'América - MG', 'Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ', '2', '1', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-07 19:30:00', 'Gama - DF', 'Ceará - CE', '0', '2', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-07 20:30:00', 'Aquidauanense Futebol Clube - MS', 'Bahia de Feira - BA', '1', '0', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-14 20:30:00', 'Bahia de Feira - BA', 'Aquidauanense Futebol Clube - MS', '2', '0', '2012']\n\n=== data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv ===\ncols: ['datetime', 'home_team', 'away_team', 'home_goal', 'away_goal', 'season', 'stage']\n['2013-02-12 20:15:00', 'Nacional (URU)', 'Barcelona-EQU', '2', '2', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-02-13 22:00:00', 'Boca Juniors', 'Toluca', '1', '2', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-02-19 23:45:00', 'Toluca', 'Nacional (URU)', '2', '3', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-02-27 19:45:00', 'Barcelona-EQU', 'Boca Juniors', '1', '2', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-03-07 00:15:00', 'Toluca', 'Barcelona-EQU', '1', '1', '2013', 'group stage']\n\n","metadata":{"output":"=== data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv ===\ncols: ['round', 'datetime', 'home_team', 'away_team', 'home_goal', 'away_goal', 'season']\n['1', '2012-03-07 16:00:00', 'Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ', 'América - MG', '0', '0', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-14 20:30:00', 'América - MG', 'Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ', '2', '1', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-07 19:30:00', 'Gama - DF', 'Ceará - CE', '0', '2', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-07 20:30:00', 'Aquidauanense Futebol Clube - MS', 'Bahia de Feira - BA', '1', '0', '2012']\n['1', '2012-03-14 20:30:00', 'Bahia de Feira - BA', 'Aquidauanense Futebol Clube - MS', '2', '0', '2012']\n\n=== data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv ===\ncols: ['datetime', 'home_team', 'away_team', 'home_goal', 'away_goal', 'season', 'stage']\n['2013-02-12 20:15:00', 'Nacional (URU)', 'Barcelona-EQU', '2', '2', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-02-13 22:00:00', 'Boca Juniors', 'Toluca', '1', '2', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-02-19 23:45:00', 'Toluca', 'Nacional (URU)', '2', '3', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-02-27 19:45:00', 'Barcelona-EQU', 'Boca Juniors', '1', '2', '2013', 'group stage']\n['2013-03-07 00:15:00', 'Toluca', 'Barcelona-EQU', '1', '1', '2013', 'group stage']\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, sys\ncsv.field_size_limit(10**9)\n\ndef peek(path, n=5):\n    print(f\"=== {path} ===\")\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        r = csv.reader(f)\n        header = next(r)\n        rows = []\n        for i, row in enumerate(r):\n            if i >= n: break\n            rows.append(row)\n    print(\"cols:\", header)\n    for row in rows: print(row)\n    print()\n\npeek('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\npeek('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nEOF","time":{"start":1788254521926,"end":1788254521929}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Both `mcp` (official MCP SDK) and `pandas` are installed. Let me also check pytest-bdd since the task asks for BDD (Gherkin) tests. Let me try installing pytest-bdd too.\n\nActually, let me plan the architecture first:\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/          # or flat modules in current dir\n├── server.py                  # MCP server entry point (FastMCP)\n├── data_loader.py             # Load & normalize all 6 CSVs\n├── models.py                  # Dataclasses for Match, Player, etc.\n├── team_normalizer.py         # Team name normalization\n├── queries.py                 # Query functions (match, team, player, competition, stats)\n├── tests/\n│   ├── conftest.py\n│   ├── test_match_queries.py  # BDD-style with pytest-bdd\n│   ├── test_team_queries.py\n│   ├── test_player_queries.py\n│   ├── test_competition_queries.py\n│   ├── test_stats.py\n│   └── test_mcp_server.py     # MCP tool-level integration tests\n```\n\nThe TASK says \"Write all code files to the current directory\" — so keep everything in the current dir (can have subdirs like `tests/`).\n\nAlso from prompts.txt (which we're told to ignore, but it hints the \"sample\" methodology): BDD GWT structured PyTest. The TASK.md says use BDD test scenarios (gherkin). pytest-bdd would be perfect. Let me install pytest-bdd.\n\nKey design decisions:\n\n1. **Data loading**: Use pandas to load CSVs, normalize into a common `Match` dataclass:\n   - `match_id`, `date` (datetime), `competition`, `season`, `stage/round`, `home_team` (normalized), `away_team` (normalized), `home_goals`, `away_goals`, `stadium`, `home_state`, `away_state`, `source_file`\n   - Keep optional fields: corners, shots, attacks (from BR-Football-Dataset)\n\n2. **Team name normalization**:\n   - Strip state suffixes: \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"Palmeiras\"\n   - Handle \"América - MG\" → \"América\" (Copa do Brasil format)\n   - Handle full names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → \"Corinthians\"? Actually in the novo_campeonato file, names like \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" appear. Let me check.\n   - Unicode normalization: \"Sao Paulo\" vs \"São Paulo\" — normalize accents for comparison (unicodedata NFKD strip accents) but display the accented version.\n   - Build a canonical team registry: map all variants to a canonical name.\n\n3. **Player queries**: FIFA data with name/club/nationality/position/overall.\n\n4. **Standings**: compute from Brasileirão matches per season (3 pts win).\n\n5. **MCP server**: Use `mcp.server.fastmcp.FastMCP` with tools:\n   - `search_matches` (team, opponent, date_from, date_to, competition, season, limit)\n   - `head_to_head` (team_a, team_b)\n   - `team_stats` (team, season, competition, home_away)\n   - `search_players` (name, nationality, club, position, min_overall, limit, sort)\n   - `top_players_at_club` (club)\n   - `standings` (competition, season)\n   - `biggest_wins` (competition, season, limit)\n   - `average_goals` (competition, season)\n   - `home_away_advantage` (competition)\n   - `derbies` (season)\n   - `last_match_between` (team_a, team_b)\n   - `team_competitions` (team)\n   - `compare_seasons` (season_a, season_b)\n   - `best_home_record` / `best_away_record` (season)\n   - `relegated_teams` (season) - bottom 4 of standings\n   - `champion` (competition, season)\n   - `championship_bracket`? \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\" — finals: find final round matches of Copa do Brasil / Libertadores.\n\nLet me check the data more to understand formats:\n\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv: home_team \"Palmeiras-SP\", goals int, season int, round int\n- Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv: round \"1\" (string, e.g. \"1\", \"final\"?), team names like \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\", \"América - MG\"\n- Libertadores_Matches.csv: stage \"group stage\", goals as strings \"2\"\n- BR-Football-Dataset.csv: tournament \"Copa do Brasil\", teams \"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\" (no accents!), goals floats \"1.0\", date \"2023-09-24\", ht_result \"DRAW/WON/LOST\"\n- novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv: \"Athletico-PR\", \"Grêmio\", dates 29/03/2003, Vencedor Mandante/Visitante/Empate, Arena\n- fifa_data.csv: first unnamed column, has BOM (\\ufeff), Name \"L. Messi\", Club \"FC Barcelona\", Position \"RF\"\n\nLet me look at more rows of each file to see variations, e.g. what rounds look like in Copa do Brasil (final), stages in Libertadores, tournaments in BR-Football-Dataset.\n\nAlso, note pandas 3.0.5 was installed (that's a recent version — pandas 3.0!). Careful with API changes in pandas 3.0. Things like `df.applymap` removed, etc. I'll use basic read_csv, filtering — should be fine.\n\nActually wait — do I even want pandas as a dependency? I could just use the csv module from stdlib. That would be simpler and avoid pandas 3.0 API issues. 18K players + 24K matches is small. Using stdlib `csv` is fine and fast. But pandas is already installed... Either works. Let me think about what's cleaner:\n\n- With pandas: read each CSV into DataFrame, convert to list of dataclasses or keep DataFrames.\n- With stdlib csv: full control, no version issues.\n\nI'll go with stdlib `csv` to minimize dependency risk (pandas 3.0 just released and might have subtle changes). Actually, hmm, pandas is useful for the FIFA file with many columns and quoted fields. But csv module handles quoted fields fine too.\n\nActually, let me use pandas — it's the natural tool, it's installed, and reading is straightforward. But pandas 3.0: `read_csv` with `encoding='utf-8-sig'` for BOM. Fine.\n\nHmm, but actually there's a subtlety: the spec says \"knowledge graph interface\". The overview says \"provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data\". This might suggest building a graph (nodes/edges) — like the prompts.txt sample says \"Use Neo4j\". But TASK.md itself doesn't require Neo4j; it says MCP server with knowledge-graph interface. The success criteria are about queries. I'll interpret \"knowledge graph interface\" loosely: the MCP server exposes tools over the data, and I can structure the query layer with entities (teams, players, matches, competitions) and relationships (head-to-head, club-membership). A full Neo4j dependency is optional (\"Optional APIs\" section doesn't mention Neo4j). I'll not use Neo4j — keep it self-contained with an in-memory model, and document it.\n\nWait, but \"knowledge graph interface\" — to be safe I could provide both: an in-memory normalized relational-ish model plus expose graph-like queries. I think building tools is what matters. The task says: \"MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\" — the LLM does the NL part, server provides tools.\n\nLet me now check more details of the data files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c468251001d6BdROigKoNybC","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c4617cf001ZMOLnCV8EtIPfp"}}
