a','america','atletico','athletico','chapecoense','goias','fortaleza','botafogo','nautico','santa cruz','ponte','portuguesa','guarani','barueri','ipatinga','joinville','juventude','criciuma','avai','figueirense','paysandu','csa','santo andre','brasil']):\n        print(repr(c))\nprint(\"---- total clubs:\", len(clubs))\n\n# Gabriel Barbosa search\ngb = [(r['Name'], r['Club'], r['Overall']) for r in prows if 'Barbosa' in r['Name']]\nprint(\"Barbosa players:\", gb[:10])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788254615165,"end":1788254615181}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Very informative:\n- FIFA data doesn't have \"Gabriel Barbosa\" (it's FIFA 19 era data, 2018-2019). It has \"Gabriel Barbosa\" as... let me search for \"Gabriel\" names later. Not a problem.\n- FIFA Brazilian clubs: Grêmio, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Santos, Internacional, Botafogo, Bahia, Vitória, Atlético Paranaense, Chapecoense, Ceará Sporting Club, Sport Club do Recife, América FC (Minas Gerais), Paraná, Vasco... Let me check Vasco, Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo in the fifa clubs.\n\nWait — \"Top clubs of Brazilian players\" doesn't include Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo! Interesting. Let me check whether those clubs exist in fifa_data at all (maybe they have no Brazilian players? No wait, that's weird). Actually FIFA 19 does have Flamengo etc. Let me check the club list more carefully.\n\nAlso note: FIFA data doesn't have \"Gabriel Barbosa\" — the spec's example \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" — search by name would return no results, but maybe there's \"G. Barbosa\"? Let me check.\n\nNow, design decisions:\n\n**Team normalization** — the hard part. Variants:\n- \"Palmeiras-SP\" (Brasileirao file, and Copa \"Palmeiras - SP\"?)\n- \"América - MG\" (Copa do Brasil format: \"Name - ST\")\n- \"Palmeiras\" (Libertadores mostly without suffix? \"Barcelona-EQU\" has country suffix EQU; Brazilian teams in Libertadores? Let me check)\n- \"Sao Paulo\" / \"Sao Paulo FC\"? (BR-Football: unaccented, e.g. \"Sao Paulo\")\n- \"Grêmio\" (accented in novo)\n- FIFA: \"Grêmio\", \"Sport Club do Recife\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Paranaense\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\"\n\nStrategy for canonical names:\n1. Create a normalization function `normalize_team(name)` that:\n   - Strips parentheticals: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → \"Boavista Sport Club - RJ\"\n   - Strips trailing \" - ST\" or \"-ST\" suffix (state): → \"Boavista Sport Club\"\n   - Handles country suffixes in Libertadores: \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Barcelona-EQU\" — these are non-Brazilian clubs mostly. For Brazilian teams in Libertadores, check what format they use. Let me check: e.g. does Libertadores have \"Palmeiras\" or \"Palmeiras-BRA\"? I'll check.\n   - Unicode-fold for comparison: strip accents, lowercase → key\n2. A canonical alias map for common Brazilian clubs mapping to a canonical display name (accented):\n   - \"corinthians\" → Corinthians; also \"sport club corinthians paulista\" → Corinthians\n   - \"gremio\" / \"gremio fbpa\"? etc.\n   - \"saopaulo\" → São Paulo; \"sao paulo fc\" → São Paulo\n   - \"atletico paranaense\", \"athletico-pr\", \"athletico paranaense\", \"atletico-pr\" → Athletico-PR (renamed 2019 from Atlético-PR to Athletico-PR; keep canonical \"Athletico Paranaense\"? For matching across files, key = \"atleticoparanaense\" for both)\n   - \"atletico-mg\", \"atletico mineiro\" → Atlético Mineiro\n   - \"america mg\", \"america fc (minas gerais)\" → América Mineiro\n   - \"ceara sporting club\", \"ceara\" → Ceará\n   - \"sport club do recife\", \"sport\", \"sport-pe\", \"sport recife\" → Sport Recife (but \"Sport\" in novo; \"Sport-PE\" in Brasileirao)\n   - \"vasco\", \"vasco da gama\" → Vasco da Gama\n   - \"botafogo\", \"botafogo-rj\", \"botafogo pb\"? — careful: Botafogo-PB (Paraíba) exists in Copa do Brasil! \"Botafogo - PB\". So state suffix matters for disambiguation. Hmm.\n\nDisambiguation issue: \"Botafogo - PB\" vs \"Botafogo - RJ\". If I strip the state suffix blindly, Botafogo-PB merges with Botafogo-RJ. In Copa do Brasil there are many small clubs. Similarly \"América - MG\", \"América - RN\", \"América - SC\"? and \"Atlético - GO\"? Wait, Copa uses \"América - MG\" format.\n\nApproach: strip suffix BUT keep a map of special cases where the suffix distinguishes clubs:\n- \"Botafogo - PB\" → \"Botafogo-PB\" (distinct from Botafogo of RJ)\n- \"América - RN\" → \"América-RN\", \"América - MG\" → \"América Mineiro\"...\n\nHmm, but this could get complicated. Simpler robust approach:\n\nFor each raw team name, compute:\n- `key` = folded (accent-stripped, lowercased, spaces removed) name after stripping parenthetical content and trailing state/country code.\n- Maintain alias table mapping keys → canonical name.\n\nFor names where the state code is needed for uniqueness (Botafogo-PB vs Botafogo), include the state in the key: e.g. \"botafogopb\" → \"Botafogo-PB\" (Paraíba) while \"botafogo\" → \"Botafogo\".\n\nWhich clubs need this? Known Brazilian same-name clubs:\n- Botafogo (RJ) vs Botafogo-PB (PB)\n- América (MG), América-RN, América-SC, América-CE? (América-CE exists: \"América (CE)\")\n- Atlético (MG), Atlético-GO, Atlético-PR? — but these are usually called \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Goianiense\", \"Atlético Paranaense\" in most datasets. In novo: \"Atlético-GO\" and \"Atlético-MG\" and \"Athletico-PR\". Hmm! novo has \"Atlético-GO\" and \"Atlético-MG\". If I strip the suffix, both become \"Atlético\". Bad!\n\nSo the state suffix MUST be part of the identity for disambiguation in cases like:\n- Atlético-MG vs Atlético-GO vs Atlético-PR (Athletico-PR)\n- América-MG vs América-RN\n- Botafogo-RJ vs Botafogo-PB? (Botafogo-PB in Copa do Brasil as \"Botafogo - PB\"?)\n\nLet me instead NOT strip state suffixes blindly. Instead:\n\n**Canonicalization strategy**: keep the state suffix when it's ambiguous,