 \"América - RN\" appear. So I need state-aware aliases for América: \"americamg\" → \"América Mineiro\", \"americarn\" → \"América-RN\". So the alias table should be applied to the full name including suffix, BEFORE stripping. Then fallback strip.\n\nOrder:\n1. fold(name) with parentheticals removed first? \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → remove parenthetical → \"Boavista Sport Club - RJ\" → fold → \"boavistasportclubrj\" → alias? Add specific alias for this? It's a tiny club; generic fallback: strip \"- RJ\" → \"Boavista Sport Club\" → \"Boavista\". Actually there's also \"Boavista\" in BR-Football? Maybe. Fine.\n2. So: canonical_key algorithm:\n   a. Remove parenthetical content.\n   b. Trim.\n   c. Fold check against alias table (on folded full string).\n   d. If not in alias table, strip trailing state/country code: regex `[-–]\\s?(SP|RJ|MG|...|[A-Z]{2,3})$` — careful: \"Barcelona-EQU\" → strip \"EQU\" → \"Barcelona\" (Ecuadorian club). That's fine for our purposes (non-Brazilian clubs are mostly only in Libertadores).\n   e. Fold again, check alias table.\n   f. Result is a key; display name = prettified from a key→display map (or title-case the base name).\n\nActually simpler: two-level lookup:\n```\nALIASES = {\n  # folded full name → canonical key\n  \"sportclubcorinthianspaulista\": \"corinthians\",\n  \"corinthians\": \"corinthians\",\n  \"saopaulo\": \"sao paulo\",  # key with space\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm, let me define canonical names WITH proper display (accents), and keys as folded versions.\n\nPlan: `TeamRegistry`:\n- `canonical(name) -> Team` with Team(key, display, state, country).\n- ALIAS map (folded → canonical key), covering all variants I find in the data.\n- Fallback generic normalizer for unmatched names.\n\nThen `resolve_team(query)`: user says \"Corinthians\" or \"sport club corinthains paulista\" or \"Timão\"? (No, keep it reasonable.) Fold query, check alias map; also do prefix/substring matching to be forgiving (\"Flamengo\" matches \"Flamengo-RJ\"? fold(\"Flamengo-RJ\") = \"flamengorj\" — the alias table handles it).\n\nFor fuzzy matching when the query isn't an exact alias: search all known team keys for substring containment (query_fold in key or key in query_fold), e.g. \"Palmeiras\" → \"palmeiras\". \"Sao Paulo\" → \"sao paulo\". \"Athletico\" → matches both \"athleticoparanaense\" and maybe \"atleticogoianiense\"? Substring \"athletico\" ⊂ \"athleticoparanaense\" yes; \"atletico\" (folded without h) ⊂ \"atleticogoianiense\" and \"atleticomineiro\". For \"Which team scored most goals\" style queries we use exact team param anyway.\n\nI'll implement:\n1. `fold(s)`: lowercase, strip accents (NFKD, drop combining marks), remove punctuation/dots, collapse spaces.\n2. `strip_state(name)`: remove parenthetical + trailing state code.\n3. `ALIASES`: dict of folded-full → canonical key. Built from a curated table of Brazilian clubs + automatically extended? Automatic: for every raw team name encountered during load, compute key via generic rule; store key → canonical display (the most \"common\" raw variant).\n\nBut automatic display might pick \"América - MG\" as display for key \"america\"... The curated alias table fixes known clubs. For uncurated, use generic.\n\nLet me enumerate what really matters for the spec examples: Flamengo, Fluminense, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo, Santos, Grêmio, Cruzeiro, Atlético Mineiro, Internacional, Vasco, Botafogo, Athletico Paranaense, Coritiba, Bahia, Sport, Ceará, Fortaleza, Vitória, Goiás, Chapecoense... plus FIFA club variants: \"Sport Club do Recife\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\", \"Atlético Paranaense\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\", \"Santos\", \"Grêmio\", \"Botafogo\", \"Bahia\", \"Internacional\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Fluminense\", \"Vitória\", \"Chapecoense\", \"Paraná\".\n\nLet me check FIFA clubs for Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo, Vasco:\n\nActually the earlier grep showed Brazilian clubs list didn't include Flamengo/Palmeiras/Corinthians/São Paulo/Vasco — because FIFA 19 didn't license those clubs? No wait — FIFA 19 (Sofifa) has Brazilian clubs but with fake-ish generic names? Actually in FIFA 19, Brazilian clubs were NOT fully licensed; players had initials like \"L. Messi\". Brazilian league clubs appear with real names but generic players? Hmm, in FIFA 19 database (sofifa), Brazilian clubs like Flamengo exist but squad players are mostly fake. Actually let me just check.\n\nAlso check \"Vasco\" in fifa clubs. Let me also check what other clubs exist. And check Brasileirao file team list (with -SP suffixes), and Libertadores Brazilian team name formats.\n\nLet me run these","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c47e845001R8hVSGZ3o45yDN","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c46f7c90010OcSxyQhUGwEiJ"}}
