score but different date, dedup by season+teams+score is risky (same pairing+score can occur twice in a season legitimately? same venue pairing occurs once per season normally (double round-robin = each venue once). So (season, home_key, away_key) is ~unique within Serie A. But Copa do Brasil has TWO LEGS with same home team (e.g. \"América - MG\" hosts Boavista twice in round 1: rows 2 and... yes rows 1&2: Boavista home then América home. Row 1: Boavista home vs América... wait rows: \"Boavista... - RJ\" home vs \"América - MG\" away; then \"América - MG\" home vs Boavista. Each hosts once. But 2013+ format has 2 legs per tie: pair A home twice? Round 1 rows show Boavista home, then América home — one each. OK single round per pairing mostly, but later rounds are 2-legged: team X home vs Y, and Y home vs X — still one each per pairing-direction. But SAME pairing-direction twice can happen in copa? \"Santos 2-0 Flamengo\" and later \"Santos 3-1 Flamengo\" both at Santos' home? In 2-legged ties each team hosts once. Penalty shootouts aside, I think (season, home_key, away_key) is mostly unique but not guaranteed (e.g., abandoned matches replayed).\n  \n  SAFEST dedup: exact tuple (date, home_key, away_key, home_goals, away_goals) → removes true duplicates across files while keeping legitimately different matches. For standings, double-count risk: same match in two files with same teams+score but slightly different date (data error) → double count in standings. Mitigate: standings uses ONE source per (competition, season) — the source preference table. This is clean and predictable:\n  \n  **Standings/match source preference per competition-season:**\n  - Brasileirão 2003-2011: novo\n  - Brasileirão 2012-2019: Brasileirao_Matches (or novo — same thing; Brasileirao_Matches is the dedicated file)\n  - Brasileirão 2020-2022: Brasileirao_Matches (2022 has 81 NA — hmm, standings for 2022 would be incomplete ~299 scored matches. BR-Football has 379 scored for 2022. Use BR-Football for 2022? But then match-search still shows Brasileirao_Matches rows with NA... \n\n  Alternative cleaner: for the unified Brasileirão, per season choose the source with the MOST scored matches:\n  - 2003-2011: novo\n  - 2012-2021: Brasileirao_Matches (380 scored each season except 2016: 379)\n  - 2022: BR-Football (379 scored vs Brasileirao_Matches 299 scored)\n  - 2023: BR-Football (377)\n  This \"max scored coverage per season\" rule is data-driven and simple. For match search across sources, I'll use the SAME season-source selection (unified competition = one source per season) PLUS include non-duplicate extras from other sources? No — keep it simple and consistent: unified Brasileirão uses exactly one source per season (max coverage rule). Document it. The BR-Football extra stats (corners etc.) still available via enrichment join for the seasons where the chosen source is BR-Football, and via joining for other sources too (enrich regardless — join on date+teams when available).\n\n  Actually wait — but then \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" works (BR-Football 2023). \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\" — all seasons 2003-2023 from chosen sources. Duplicates avoided. \n\n- Copa do Brasil: \n  - 2012: file only\n  - 2013: file only\n  - 2014-2021: file (120/season) vs BR-Football (~110-140) — file has more most seasons (139 vs BR-Football 2015=139 same; 2016: 162 vs 147 file wins; 2017: 120 vs 105; 2018: 120 vs 111; 2019: 120 vs 117; 2020: 120 vs 117; 2021: 108 vs 111 — brf wins 2021!). Max-coverage rule: 2021 → BR-Football (111), else file.\n  - 2022-2023: BR-Football only.\n- Serie B, Serie C: BR-Football only (all seasons).\n- Libertadores: file only.\n\nBUT: BR-Football Copa 2021 = 111 rows — includes the 16 NA-goal rows? No wait, the NA rows were in the Copa FILE (Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv 2021). BR-Football has no bad goals. OK.\n\nMax-scored-coverage rule handles everything automatically. \n\n**2021 Serie A = 491 rows in BR-Football?** — that's >380, meaning duplicates or playoffs... Serie A 2021 had 38 rounds, 380 matches. 491 suggests the dataset double-counts some matches (maybe two rows for same match with corrected stats). But Brasileirao_Matches 2021 = 380 clean → chosen source is Brasileirao_Matches for 2021 anyway. For Serie B 2021 = 446 (>380!) — hmm, Serie B 2021 had 20 teams = 380. 446 rows = duplicates. And 2020 Serie B = 302 (<380, incomplete COVID). Series C is a knockout+group format with variable counts — fine.\n\nFor Serie B standings 2021, duplicate rows would corrupt the table. Mitigation: within a source, dedup exact (date, home, away, goals) — if the 446 contains ~66 exact dupes, dedup fixes it. Let me check Serie B 2021 duplicates. Also there could be same (date,home,away) with different goals (stat corrections) — then dedup by (date, home, away) keeping first? Risky but reasonable. Let me check empirically.\n\nAlso 2021 Serie A 491 — same check.\n\nLet me quickly check dup patterns in BR-Football, then finalize the design. Also dump ALL team names for alias curation.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c4ade97001dP3urEuCiEFPFW","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c4a832f001PsU5RmOdj2wXmB"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788254813733,"sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a5a76b9a278fef87","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\ncsv.field_size_limit(10**9)\ndef fold(s):\n    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s)\n    s = ''.join(c for c in s if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n    return s.lower().strip()\ndef compact(s):\n    return ''.join(ch for ch in fold(s) if ch.isalnum())\n\nallnames = {}\ndef add(names, src):\n    for n in names:\n        n = n.strip()\n        if n: allnames.setdefault(n, set()).add(src)\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbra = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nadd([r['home_team'] for r in bra]+[r['away_team'] for r in bra], 'bra')\ncopa = load('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nadd([r['home_team'] for r in copa]+[r['away_team'] for r in copa], 'copa')\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nadd([r['home_team'] for r in lib]+[r['away_team'] for r in lib], 'lib')\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nadd([r['home'] for r in brf]+[r['away'] for r in brf], 'brf')\nnovo = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nadd([r['Equipe_mandante'] for r in novo]+[r['Equipe_visitante'] for r in novo], 'novo')\n\nprint(\"total distinct raw names:\", len(allnames))\n# group by compact-with-state-stripped to find collisions/variants\nimport re\ndef strip_state(n):\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\\s*', ' ', n).strip()\n    n = re.sub(r'[-–]\\s*[A-Za-z]{2,3}$', '', n).strip()\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s+[A-Za-z]{2,3}$', '', n).strip()\n    return n\ngroups = {}\nfor n in allnames:\n    groups.setdefault(compact(strip_state(n)), []).append(n)\n# show groups with many variants or cross-source\ninteresting = 0\nfor k, v in sorted(groups.items()):\n    srcs = set()\n    for n in v: srcs |= allnames[n]\n    if len(v) >= 3 or ('bra' in srcs and 'novo' in srcs) or ('copa' in srcs and 'brf' in srcs):\n        print(f\"{k}: {sorted(set(v))}\")\n        interesting += 1\nprint(\"interesting groups:\", interesting)\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96"},"output":"total distinct raw names: 725\n4dejulho: ['4 de Julho - PI', '4 de Julho EC']\nabc: ['A.b.c. - RN', 'ABC', 'ABC - RN', 'Abc - RN']\naguianegra: ['Aguia Negra - MS', 'Aguia Negra-MS', 'Águia Negra - MS']\naltos: ['Altos', 'Altos - PI']\namadense: ['Amadense - SE', 'Amadense EC']\namerica: ['America - MG', 'America MG', 'America RN', 'America-MG', 'América - MG', 'América - RN', 'América-MG', 'América-RN']\namericano: ['Americano - RJ', 'Americano RJ']\nanapolina: ['Anapolina', 'Anapolina - GO']\nanapolis: ['Anapolis FC', 'Anápolis - GO']\naparecidense: ['Aparecidense', 'Aparecidense - GO', 'Aparecidense GO']\naquidauanense: ['Aquidauanense', 'Aquidauanense - MS']\nasa: ['A.s.a. - AL', 'ASA', 'ASA AL', 'Asa - AL']\nathleticoparanaense: ['Athletico Paranaense', 'Athletico Paranaense - PR']\natletico: ['Atletico - ES', 'Atletico - PR', 'Atletico-GO', 'Atletico-MG', 'Atletico-PR', 'Atlético - AC', 'Atlético - BA', 'Atlético - GO', 'Atlético - MG', 'Atlético - PR', 'Atlético-GO', 'Atlético-MG', 'Atlético-PR']\natleticomineiro: ['Atletico Mineiro', 'Atlético Mineiro - MG']\natleticoparanaense: ['Atletico Paranaense', 'Atlético Paranaense - PR']\naudax: ['Audax - SP', 'Audax SP']\navai: ['Avai', 'Avai-SC', 'Avaí', 'Avaí - SC']\navenida: ['Avenida', 'Avenida - RS']\nbahia: ['Bahia', 'Bahia - BA', 'Bahia-BA']\nbahiadefeira: ['Bahia de Feira', 'Bahia de Feira - BA']\nbangu: ['Bangu', 'Bangu - RJ']\nbarbalha: ['Barbalha', 'Barbalha - CE']\nboa: ['Boa', 'Boa - MG']\nboavista: ['Boavista', 'Boavista - RJ', 'Boavista RJ']\nbotafogo: ['Botafogo', 'Botafogo - PB', 'Botafogo - RJ', 'Botafogo PB', 'Botafogo RJ', 'Botafogo SP', 'Botafogo-RJ']\nbragantino: ['Bragantino'