; \"Fluminense\" self; \"Internacional\" self; \"Vitória\" self; \"Chapecoense\" self; \"Paraná\" self; \"Ceará Sporting Club\"→ceara; \"Sport Club do Recife\"→sportrecife; \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\"→americamineiro. And FIFA foreign clubs: \"Atlético Madrid\" → \"atleticomadrid\" unclaimed → own key ✓; \"Santos Laguna\" → \"santoslaguna\" ✓ (no collision since compact differs from \"santos\"); \"Club América\" → \"clubamerica\" ✓; \"América de Cali\" → \"americadecali\" ✓ (Libertadores too); \"Atlético Nacional\" → \"atléticonacional\"→\"atleticonacional\" ✓; \"Peñarol\" → \"penarol\" ✓ (hmm — \"Peñarol\" (URU, FIFA + Libertadores) and \"Penarol - AM\" (brf) → \"penarolam\" distinct ✓).\n+ Libertadores foreign aliases: nacionaluru→nacionaluru (self), nacionalpar→self, guaranipar→self, barcelonaecu→self (compact(\"Barcelona-EQU\")=\"barcelonaequ\"!! wait: \"Barcelona-EQU\" fold → \"barcelona-equi\"? NO — fold strips accents only; \"EQU\" → \"equ\" lowercase → compact \"barcelonaequ\". So alias key is \"barcelonaequ\"!). Let me recompute these compacts carefully:\n  - \"Barcelona-EQU\" → barcelonaequ\n  - \"Delfín-EQU\" → delfinequ\n  - \"Nacional (URU)\" → nacionaluru\n  - \"Nacional-URU\" → nacionaluru (same compact!) ✓ merge naturally\n  - \"Nacional (PAR)\" → nacionalpar\n  - \"Guaraní (PAR)\" → guaranipar; \"Guaraní-PAR\" → guaranipar ✓\n  - \"River Plate-URU\" → riverplateuru\n  - \"Olimpia-PAR\" → olimpiapar\n  - \"Libertad-PAR\" → libertadpar\n  - \"Universitario (PER)\" → universitarioper; \"Universitario-PER\" → universitarioper ✓\n  - \"Trujillanos (VEN)\" → trujillanosven\n  - \"The Strongest\" → thestrongest ✓\n  - \"LDU\" → ldu ✓\n  - \"Ind. Santa Fe\" → ind Santafe → compact \"indsantafe\" ✓\n  - \"Newells Old Boys\" → newellsoldboys ✓\n  These can be generic (unclaimed bases with no suffix → base key) EXCEPT they'd collide: \"Nacional (URU)\" — remove parens → \"Nacional\" → base \"nacional\" — COLLIDES with \"Nacional - AM\"→\"nacionalam\"? No wait: bare \"Nacional\" vs \"Nacional - AM\": if I strip suffix+parens for base, \"Nacional (URU)\" base = \"nacional\" and \"Nacional - AM\" base = \"nacional\" too! Both unclaimed → \"Nacional (URU)\" no state → key \"nacional\"; \"Nacional - AM\" has state AM → key \"nacionalam\". So Nacional-URU and Nacional-PAR and bare Nacional ALL → \"nacional\" — THREE different clubs merged! Need ALIASES: nacionaluru→nacionaluru, nacionalpar→nacionalpar (mapped to themselves i.e. in CLUBS so base-strip never happens). Similarly \"Guaraní (PAR)\"/\"Guaraní-PAR\" vs Brazilian \"Guarani\": if unclaimed, all → \"guarani\"... but guarani IS claimed (Guarani SP). \"Guaraní (PAR)\": base \"guarani\" claimed by SP club; state? none (paren form) → my state rule: state=None → return canonical → WRONG (Paraguayan club maps to Brazilian Guarani)! So ALIASES must catch compact_full \"guaranipar\" FIRST → own key \"guaranipar\" ✓. Same for \"riverplateuru\" (River Plate-URU vs River Plate ARG): \"River Plate-URU\" compact_full \"riverplateuru\" → ALIASES → own key ✓; bare \"River Plate\" → riverplate (ARG) ✓.\n  So rule: parenthetical \"(XXX)\" forms — the country code is in the PARENS. My compact_full KEEPS parens content: \"Nacional (URU)\" → \"nacionaluru\" ✓. So alias entries: nacionaluru→nacionaluru, nacionalpar→nacionalpar, guaranipar→guaranipar, universitarioper→universitarioper, trujillanosven→trujillanosven, barcelonaequ→barcelonaequ, delfinequ→delfinequ, riverplateuru→riverplateuru, olimpiapar→olimpiapar, libertadpar→libertadpar.\n  Hmm wait — but my compact_full for \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" = \"americafcminasgerais\" → ALIASES → americamineiro ✓ planned.\n  And \"Rio Branco - Vn - ES\" → compact_full \"riobrancovnes\"?? whatever, fallback.\n\nAlso: does the state-strip regex handle \"- Vn - ES\"? `[-–\\s]\\s*[A-Za-z]{2,3}$` strips \" - ES\" → \"Rio Branco - Vn\"; another pass? Single pass leaves \"Vn\". compact \"riobrancovn\"? eh, fine.\n\nOne more: \"Sao Jose - POA\": strip \"POA\" → \"Sao Jose\" → base \"saojose\" claimed? no → key \"saojose\" — merges with \"São José - RS\" → same \"saojose\"?? \"São José - RS\" (RS club, Porto Alegre) vs \"Sao Jose - POA\" — POA = Porto Alegre — SAME CLUB! ✓ merge correct. \"Sao Jose PA\"?? — hmm \"Sao Jose PA\"... PA? There's São José-PA? Actually earlier group: saojose: ['Sao Jose - POA', 'Sao Jose PA', 'Sao Jose RS', 'São José - RS']. \"Sao Jose PA\" — PA?? weird, maybe data noise for POA (typo). Both merge to \"saojose\" — fine.\n\nOK. This design is solid. Now **display names**: canonical clubs have display from table. For auto keys, display = prettified base name (use the most common raw variant, or title-case the stripped base). I'll store: registry[key] = {display, states, variants[raw...], sources} and pick display = most frequent raw variant that had the state suffix stripped... simpler: display = stripped base name as-is (preserving accents from whichever raw form seen first / most common). E.g. key \"criciuma\" — canonical display \"Criciúma\" from table ✓ (criciuma in majors). Key \"caldensemg\" → display \"Caldense\" (base stripped). OK.\n\n**Now the season-bucketing fix for BR-Football**: check Jan-Mar matches belong to previous season. Verify empirically: count rows by month for Serie A 2020/2021.\n\nAlso, what about novo \"Vasco\" (bare) — alias \"vasco\"→vascodagama ✓ in list. And Libertadores \"Vasco\" ✓ same alias. And FIFA \"Vasco\"? not present. OK.\n\n**One more check**: what does \"Atletico - PR\" in Copa map to — atleticoparanaense ✓ (alias). \"Athletico Paranaense - PR\"? group athleticoparanaense: ['Athletico Paranaense', 'Athletico Paranaense - PR'] — compact \"athleticoparanaensepr\" → after athletico→atletico replace → \"atleticoparanaensepr\" → ALIASES ✓.\n\nAnd BR-Football \"Athletico Paranaense\" → compact \"athleticoparanaense\" → replace → \"atleticoparanaense\" → CLUBS self ✓.\n\nWhat about \"Athletic Club MG\" (brf)? → \"athleticclubmg\" — hmm Athletic Club (MG) is a real club (Série C). compact_full \"athleticclubmg\" — contains \"athletic\"... my replace('athletico','atletico') doesn't touch \"athleticclub\" (no 'athletico' substring — \"athleticclub\" has \"athletic\"+\"c\"...) \"athletico\" ≠ \"athleticclub\" ✓ untouched. Unclaimed base \"athleticclub\"... wait strip \" MG\" → base \"Athletic Club\" → key \"athleticclub\" ✓ fine.\n\nWait, one more important thing — the athletico→atletico replace must run BEFORE alias lookup? I said: alias(c) first, then alias(c2). Hmm — \"Athletico Paranaense\" compact \"athleticoparanaense\": first lookup \"athleticoparanaense\" in ALIASES — I'll include BOTH spellings in ALIASES to be safe (athleticoparanaense→atleticoparanaense, athleticopr→atleticoparanaense, athletico→atleticoparanaense). Then the replace pass becomes unnecessary! Just put both spellings in ALIASES. Simpler — skip the replace logic, enumerate both. ✓\n\n**Also FIFA players club matching**: \"Club\" column → resolve to team key for cross-file queries (\"Which players play for Flamengo\" → players where club_key == flamengo; also club containing?). I'll resolve FIFA clubs through the same team_key() and index players by club key. Plus substring fallback for club search (e.g. \"Recife\"?). Keep: exact key match OR raw club substring match.\n\n**Player name search**: \"Gabriel Barbosa\" → substring match on Name (\"Gabriel Barbosa\" not present; \"G. Barbosa\"? not present either — search returns players whose name contains the query, case/accent-insensitive; also try without spaces \"gabrielbarbosa\" ⊂ compact(name)?). I'll do: normalize query; match if compact(name) contains compact(query) OR fuzzy (difflib ratio > 0.8?) — keep it simple: substring on compacted names + also match individual tokens. \"Who is Neymar?\" → \"Neymar Jr\" ✓ compact contains \"neymar\".\n\n**Season bucketing verification needed**: BR-Football Jan-Mar → previous season. Let me check months. Serie A 2021: 491 rows; how many in Jan-Feb 2021? ~111 would confirm. Then 2020: 264 + 111 = 375. Also Copa do Brasil 2021=111: Copa 2020 final rounds played Apr 2021?? Hmm Copa 2020 (won by Palmeiras, final May 2021!). Copa 2021 also ran. If I re-bucket Jan-Mar matches to prev season: Copa 2021 would lose ~X rows and 2020 gains them. Copa do Brasil 2020 had 117 in file (the cup file!) vs brf 117 — fine. Let me just check month distribution.\n\nThen for **choosing per-season source**: \"max scored matches\" rule after re-bucketing. For Serie A 2020: bra file has 380 scored (2012-2022 incl 2020: 380) → bra wins anyway. For 2021: bra 380 vs brf (491 - Jan/Feb 2021 rows...). Re-bucketed brf 2021 = ~380 + Copa... whatever, bra 380 wins or ties; tie → prefer dedicated file. Rule: prefer order [dedicated file, novo, brf] among sources with max scored count? Let me define preference order per competition: Brasileirão: [Brasileirao_Matches, novo, brf]; Copa do Brasil: [Brazilian_Cup_Matches, brf]; Serie B/C: [brf]; Libertadores: [lib file]. Selection: among sources for that season, pick the one with most SCORED matches; tie → earlier in preference order. Then merge in extra rows from other sources ONLY IF they add matches not already present (exact dedup on date+home+away+goals)? Hmm — \"Copa do Brasil 2021 file: 108 rows, 16 NA → 92 scored; brf 2021: 111 scored\" → brf wins 2021 ✓. \"Copa 2014: file 159 vs brf 43\" → file ✓.\n\nBut WAIT — there's a subtlety with the unification for match search: with one-source-per-season, Brasileirão 2012-2022 comes from bra file; novo 2012-2019 rows are dropped entirely (same matches, fewer rounds info? novo has Arena!). Arena/stadium info lost for 2012-2019. Meh — acceptable; or enrich: attach Arena from novo join (date+teams) like corners from brf. I'll do generic enrichment: brf stats (corners/shots/attacks/ht) and novo arena joined by (date, home_key, away_key) where available. \n\nHmm, actually — wait. Let me reconsider whether unification is even the right call for MATCH SEARCH vs