opa do Brasil\" (2014-2023)\n- libertadores: lib file (2013-2022)\n- serieb: brf \"Serie B\"\n- seriec: brf \"Serie C\"\n\n**Round/stage normalization**: bra file round int; novo Rodada int; copa round \"1\"-\"8\" (string); lib stage strings; brf none. Unified field `stage: str` = e.g. \"Round 22\", \"Semifinal\"...? Keep raw-ish: for leagues: f\"Round {n}\"; copa: map round number to name? Copa rounds 1-8: 1=\"First Round\"... 8=\"Final\"? Is round 8 the final? 2021 copa file: round 8, 14 matches... Let me check: Copa do Brasil finals 2012-2021: each final 2 legs = 20 matches; round 8 has 14?? Hmm. Let me check round distribution per season. If round 8 = final, 2012-2021 finals... some single-leg? Let me check. For \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" I need to identify final matches: highest round per season in cup file; Libertadores stage==\"final\". Let me check what rounds 6/7/8 correspond to (semifinal=7? quarterfinal=6?...). Round numbers: R1 334, R2 376, R3 258, R4 140, R5 123, R6 62, R7 30, R8 14. 2012-2021 = 10 seasons. R8=14 → finals: 2012-2021... 2020 final was single match? and 2021? Hmm: 2 legs x 10 = 20 ≠ 14. Unless some finals single-leg. Whatever: highest round per season = final. Also note the copa file uses \"round\" numbers where semifinal = 7, quarterfinal = 6? R7=30/10=3 per season?? Semis 2 legs x 2 ties = 4 matches/season → 40 expected. 30 → some seasons different format (2020/2021 single leg?). Eh — data is data. Map: for the cup, stage = \"Round N\" and finals = matches in the max round of each season. For nicer naming I can add a label map when round number = max round of season → \"Final\", second max → \"Semifinal\"...? Not reliable. Just report round number + label the max as \"Final(s)\".\n\nHmm wait — actually for Copa do Brasil, let me check the actual round names... the file only has numbers 1-8. Real Copa do Brasil: First Round, Second Round, Third Round, Round of 16, Quarterfinals?? Hmm 8 rounds: 1,2,3,16-avos... The 2012+ format: Round 1 (78→39 ties), Round 2, Round 3, Round of 16, Quarterfinals, Semifinals, Final. That's 7 stages. 8 rounds in data = maybe includes \"final\" split... R5=123, hmm. I'll just present \"Round 8 (final)\" as the last round. Let me empirically get max round per season and see counts. If finals are consistently 2 legs (14 ≈ 10 seasons x ~1.4)... let me check.\n\n**Libertadores finals**: stage == 'final' → 15 matches (2 legs x 10 seasons minus single-leg 2020 = 20-5?? 15... whatever).\n\n**best_records venue=home/away**: compute per team.\n\n**derbies**: known pairs (by canonical keys):\n- Fla-Flu: flamengo-fluminense\n- Clássico dos Milhões? (flamengo-vascodagama)\n- Vovô: botafogo-fluminense? botafogo-vasco\n- Majestoso: corinthians-saopaulo\n- Choque-Rei: palmeiras-saopaulo\n- Derby Paulista: palmeiras-corinthians\n- Grenal: gremio-internacional\n- Ba-Vi: bahia-vitoria\n- Re-Pa? (remo-paysandu) Clássico dos Milhões no — Re-Pa = remo-paysandu ✓\n- Clássico dos Gigantes? (vasco-saopaulo?) skip\n- Atleti-MG derby: atleticomineiro-cruzeiro (Clássico Mineiro) ✓\n- Coritiba-atleticoparanaense? \"Atlético-PR x Coritiba\" (Paradá?) — Atletiba ✓\n- Ceará-Fortaleza: Clássico-Rei ✓\n- Sport-Náutico: Clássico dos Clássicos ✓; Sport-Santa Cruz: Clássico das Multidões ✓\n- Santos-Palmeiras? no real derby name... skip.\nI'll include ~12 named derbies. \n\n**MCP integration tests**: use `mcp` client over stdio: spawn `python server.py` subprocess with stdio_client, list tools, call a few. Confirm mcp 2.1.1 API — FastMCP in mcp.server.fastmcp; stdio client in mcp.client.stdio. Let me verify quickly.\n\n**File layout** (current dir):\n```\nserver.py                     # entry point: FastMCP server, wires tools\nbrazilian_soccer/\n  __init__.py\n  models.py                   # Match, Player, TeamInfo, StandingRow dataclasses\n  normalize.py                # fold/compact, CLUBS, ALIASES, TeamRegistry, team resolution\n  loader.py                   # CSV loading, parsing, season buck