mm 2019 Copa had 91 matches: R1(40)+R2(20)+R3(20)+R4(10)+R5(16)+R6(8)+R7(4)+R8(2) = 120?? Sum: 40+20+20+10+16+8+4+2 = 120. Hmm that's 2021: {1:40, 2:20, 3:32, 4:16} — only 108, incomplete (R3 32?? 2021 had no R5+ because... data incomplete — 16 teams in R4 but no QF/SF/final rows?! Wait 2021 Copa file has rounds only 1-4?? That means the 2021 Copa file is incomplete — no quarterfinals onward! But earlier I saw NA-goal rows in 2021 round 4 (Fluminense-Criciúma...). Hmm — actually wait: 2021 Copa do Brasil: round of 16 was \"fourth stage\"?? Let me recount 2021 real format: 2021 Copa do Brasil had 92 clubs; rounds: First (Aug 2020?), ... The 2021 final: Atlético-MG vs Athletico-PR (Nov 2021). If the file's 2021 season only has rounds 1-4 (108 matches, 16 NA) — the file is missing QF/SF/Final for 2021! Hmm. But WAIT — maybe those later 2021 rounds are in the file under season 2022? No — 2022 rounds would be separate. Let me check what the max round per season is in the cup file: 2012-2020 have 8 rounds; 2021 stops at 4. So \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" → seasons 2012-2020 only (2 matches each = 18 finals). Plus brf for 2022-2023 (which includes finals? brf Copa 2022 = 117 matches — if it includes the final rounds, then for finals queries I should ALSO search brf when chosen... but brf is only chosen as source for 2022/2023 — and the finals query operates on the unified data → 2022/2023 finals present ✓ via brf source).\n\n   Hmm — but hold on: unified \"one source per season\" means for the FINALS query on 2012-2021, source = cup file (max scored). 2021 finals missing from cup file but present in brf 2021 (61 after rebucket... does brf have the 2021 final? Copa 2021 brf months: 10:4, 12:2 — the final was Nov/Dec 2021?? real final Nov 2021 2 legs. 12:2 = December 2 matches — maybe the final legs! Possibly). So for FINALS specifically, missing 2021 finals (cup file incomplete). Trade-off accepted — OR: my unification could do per-season source choice, and the \"fina