{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788255207378,"sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-88a74f4893682bf5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\ncsv.field_size_limit(10**9)\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nfor yr in ['2022','2023']:\n    months = Counter(r['date'][5:7] for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil' and r['date'][:4]==yr)\n    print(\"Copa\", yr, dict(sorted(months.items())))\n# check Flamengo-Coritiba 2022 final rows\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil' and r['date'][:4]=='2022' and {r['home'],r['away']}=={'Flamengo','Coritiba'}:\n        print(r['date'], r['home'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away'])\n# also check early-2022 rows (Jan-Mar) that would be re-bucketed to 2021\nearly = [(r['tournament'], r['date'], r['home'], r['away']) for r in brf if r['date'][:4]=='2022' and r['date'][5:7] in ('01','02','03') and r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil']\nprint(\"Copa early 2022 rows:\", len(early))\nfor e in early[:6]: print(e)\n# Serie B early 2021 rows (should be 2020 season)\nsb21 = Counter(r['date'][5:7] for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie B' and r['date'][:4]=='2021')\nprint(\"SerieB 2021 months:\", dict(sorted(sb21.items())))\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96"},"output":"Copa 2022 {'02': 17, '03': 38, '04': 14, '05': 17, '06': 9, '07': 12, '08': 6, '09': 2, '10': 2}\nCopa 2023 {'02': 16, '03': 38, '04': 32, '05': 10, '06': 6, '07': 10, '08': 2, '09': 2}\nCopa early 2022 rows: 55\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-24', 'Vitoria EC', 'GE Gloria')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-18', 'Goias', 'Criciuma')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-17', 'Real Noroeste ES', 'EC Juventude')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-17', 'CSA', 'Paysandu')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-17', 'Sao Paulo', 'Manaus')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-16', 'tuntum EC', 'Cruzeiro')\nSerieB 2021 months: {'01': 67, '05': 9, '06': 67, '07': 69, '08': 65, '09': 59, '10': 50, '11': 60}\n","metadata":{"output":"Copa 2022 {'02': 17, '03': 38, '04': 14, '05': 17, '06': 9, '07': 12, '08': 6, '09': 2, '10': 2}\nCopa 2023 {'02': 16, '03': 38, '04': 32, '05': 10, '06': 6, '07': 10, '08': 2, '09': 2}\nCopa early 2022 rows: 55\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-24', 'Vitoria EC', 'GE Gloria')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-18', 'Goias', 'Criciuma')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-17', 'Real Noroeste ES', 'EC Juventude')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-17', 'CSA', 'Paysandu')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-17', 'Sao Paulo', 'Manaus')\n('Copa do Brasil', '2022-03-16', 'tuntum EC', 'Cruzeiro')\nSerieB 2021 months: {'01': 67, '05': 9, '06': 67, '07': 69, '08': 65, '09': 59, '10': 50, '11': 60}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\ncsv.field_size_limit(10**9)\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nfor yr in ['2022','2023']:\n    months = Counter(r['date'][5:7] for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil' and r['date'][:4]==yr)\n    print(\"Copa\", yr, dict(sorted(months.items())))\n# check Flamengo-Coritiba 2022 final rows\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil' and r['date'][:4]=='2022' and {r['home'],r['away']}=={'Flamengo','Coritiba'}:\n        print(r['date'], r['home'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away'])\n# also check early-2022 rows (Jan-Mar) that would be re-bucketed to 2021\nearly = [(r['tournament'], r['date'], r['home'], r['away']) for r in brf if r['date'][:4]=='2022' and r['date'][5:7] in ('01','02','03') and r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil']\nprint(\"Copa early 2022 rows:\", len(early))\nfor e in early[:6]: print(e)\n# Serie B early 2021 rows (should be 2020 season)\nsb21 = Counter(r['date'][5:7] for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie B' and r['date'][:4]=='2021')\nprint(\"SerieB 2021 months:\", dict(sorted(sb21.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788255207373,"end":1788255207377}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The mcp 2.x API works:\n- `MCPServer(name=...)`\n- `@server.tool()` decorator with type hints\n- `await server.list_tools()` → list of Tool (name, description, input_schema)\n- `await server.call_tool(name, args)` → CallToolResult with .content (list of TextContent)\n- `server.run(\"stdio\")` — sync stdio entry\n\nNow I have everything I need. Let me plan the implementation with a todo list and write the code.\n\n### Implementation plan\n\n**Files:**\n1. `brazilian_soccer/__init__.py` — package doc, exports\n2. `brazilian_soccer/models.py` — dataclasses: Match, MatchStats, Player, TeamStat, StandingRow, CompetitionInfo, HeadToHead, etc.\n3. `brazilian_soccer/normalize.py` — fold, compact, CLUBS table, ALIASES, TeamRegistry (build from data + curated), team resolution + fuzzy search\n4. `brazilian_soccer/loader.py` — CSV parsers, date parsers, competition definitions, per-season source selection, dedup, enrichment, indexes → SoccerData\n5. `brazilian_soccer/analysis.py` — query functions over SoccerData returning result dataclasses/dicts\n6. `brazilian_soccer/formatting.py` — render spec-style text output for each result\n7. `server.py` — MCPServer wiring ~19 tools + resource; `main()` runs stdio\n8. `tests/conftest.py` — session fixtures: soccer data, MCP server instance\n9. `tests/features/*.feature` — Gherkin features (match, team, player, competition, stats, normalization, mcp server, performance)\n10. `tests/test_*.py` — step definitions bound to features\n11. `tests/test_unit_*.py`? — I'll put unit-level checks into BDD where possible; a few plain unit tests for normalize/loader edge cases (date parsing, compact)\n12. `requirements.txt`\n13. `README.md` — updated documentation\n14. `pytest.ini` or `pyproject.toml` — pytest config (asyncio mode, bdd features dir). I'll add `pytest.ini`.\n\n### Key algorithm recap (loader):\n\n```\nCOMPETITION_SOURCES = {\n  \"brasileirao\": [(\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", bra_parse), (\"novo...\", novo_parse), (\"BR-Football... Serie A\", brf_parse)],\n  \"copadobrasil\": [cup, brf-copa],\n  \"libertadores\": [lib],\n  \"serieb\": [brf-Serie B],\n  \"seriec\": [brf-Serie C],\n}\n```\n\nPer (competition, season): scored counts per source; pick max (tie → order in list); parse that source's rows for the season; skip unparseable (no goals / no date); dedup exact (date, home_key, away_key, home_goals, away_goals); create Match objects; record skipped counts.\n\nEnrichment: \n- brf stats map: (date, home_key, away_key) → MatchStats(corners, shots, attacks, ht) — for matches from non-brf sources, attach if join matches.\n- novo arena map: (date, home_key, away_key) → stadium. Hmm — dates between novo and bra disagree 70% of the time, so arena enrichment will rarely join. Fine — attach when possible.\n- Also brf has `time` (kickoff) — keep kickoff for brf-sourced matches.\n\n**Season bucketing for brf**: if month in (1,2,3) → season = year-1. (Apr-Dec → year.) Apply to ALL brf tournaments. Hmm wait — what about Copa do Brasil 2021 with matches in April (04:16)? Real Copa 2021 first round was May 11-13, 2021?? Hmm, actually 2021 Copa first round: March 2021?? Let me think: 2021 Copa do Brasil started... I recall Grêmio x AA Portuguesa May 2021. Hmm — but data shows Copa 2021 months: 03:34, 04:16, 06:32... The March-April 2021 Copa matches: these are the 2020 Copa second round (played Mar 2021) + third round (Apr 2021)?? The 2020 Copa: first round Aug 2020 (52+18=70... wait Copa 2020 brf months: 02:52, 03:18, 08:10, 09:10, 10:9, 11:14, 12:4 — so 2020: Aug-Dec 2020 (47 matches: 10+10+9+14+4) + Jan?? none + Feb 2021: 52 + Mar 2021: 18 = 70 + 47 = 117. Real Copa 2020: first round was ~55 matches (Feb-Mar 2021!), second round Apr 2021, QF/SF Nov-Dec 2020?? No wait — real 2020 Copa do Brasil: Rounds 1&2 postponed to 2021; R3+ played late 2020; final April 2021 (Gremio-Palmeiras, Apr 2021 - 2 legs Apr 28? hmm actually final was March/April 2021). Ugh — so brf's Feb-Mar 2021 Copa rows = 2020 Copa R1/R2 ✓ my re-bucket rule (Jan-Mar → prev) assigns them to 2020 ✓. April 2021 (16 matches) = 2020 Copa R2 (Apr 28-29, 2021?) or the final? My rule leaves April in 2021 — slightly wrong (2020 Copa R2 played Apr 28; final May 2021?? hmm hmm). Since the cup FILE wins for 2020 (120 scored vs brf 117) and 2021 (92 vs ~61), these brf mis-buckets never get chosen. ✓ Fine.\n\nAlso what about Serie C? runs May-Nov ✓. Serie B 2020 ran Sep 2020-Jan 2021?? Serie B 2020: started Sep 2020, ended Jan 2021? Hmm — actually Serie B 2020 finished Jan 29 2021! So brf \"2021\" Jan rows (59?? for Serie A; for B similar) → re-bucket to 2020 ✓. \n\nHmm wait — one caveat: Serie A 2021 rows in May 2021 (10): Serie A 2021 started May 29-30, 2021 ✓ stays 2021 ✓.\n\nBUT — what about Copa do Brasil 2022 (117 rows)? Months? 2022 Copa: rounds Feb?? No — 2022 Copa started... hmm, 2022 Copa do Brasil first round Feb 2022?? Hmm, actually no: 2022 Copa R1 was... I believe Feb-Mar 2022? Hmm — wait, if 2022 Copa R1 was in February-March 2022, my Jan-Mar rule re-buckets those to \"2021\" — WRONG! Let me check: Copa do Brasil 2022 first round: April 2022? Let me check the months of brf Copa 2022 rows. Real answer: 2022 Copa do Brasil first round was played Feb-Mar 2022?? I genuinely don't remember. Hmm. Let me check the data months for brf Copa 2022, and sanity check against known: Copa 2022 champion was Flamengo (beat Coritiba in final Oct 2022). If brf Copa 2022 shows months Apr-Nov, fine. Let me also double check 2023 Copa: started March 2023?? 2023 Copa R1: Feb-Mar 2023?? hmm.\n\nUgh — the Jan-Mar rule could corrupt Copa 2022/2023 (brf-chosen seasons!). Let me check months per brf Copa year in data. If 2022/2023 Copa months start in Feb/Mar, I need a smarter rule. Alternatives: per-tournament rules: for Serie A/B/C (leagues): Jan-Mar → prev season. For Copa: hmm.\n\nActually, better: make the rule DATA-DRIVEN per tournament+source: a season's matches form a contiguous block; but simplest robust: apply Jan-Mar→prev ONLY for Serie A/B/C (league calendars are Apr-Dec, confirmed). For Copa do Brasil in brf, check actual months and decide. Libertadores: not in brf at all. Let me check Copa months for 2022/2023 in brf data.\n\nReal-world facts (from memory, verify against data shape): \n- Copa do Brasil 2022: R1 Mar 2-3?? Hmm. Actually I think 2022 Copa R1 was in February... hmm no. Let me just look at the data and cross-check with the cup file / known matchups. E.g., 2022 Copa final: Flamengo 2-0 Coritiba (Nov 6? Oct 30?), 2nd leg Coritiba 1-1 Flamengo? Hmm no — 2022 final: Flamengo beat Coritiba 3-0 agg (2-0, 1-1?). And 2022 R1 featured... e.g. \"Floresta vs ...\" \n\nLet me check the data: months for brf Copa 2022 & 2023, and spot check the number of matches against the real format (2022 Copa had 92 clubs → R1: 38 matches... total 2022 Copa = 91 matches?? hmm 92 clubs: R1 46 matches? The real numbers: 2022: 92 teams; total matches ~86?). The cup FILE 2022? No — cup file only has 2012-2021. Hmm.\n\nOK let me check empirically.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c50eb48001TdwwUufjXRXD3M","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c50458a0014nkJhK46HktIat"}}
