ata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — BUG: \"serieb: 10296 matches\" and \"seriec: 10296 matches\" — identical to the total BR-Football row count (10296)! That means the season_rows bucketing is putting ALL brf rows into every tournament's competition. Looking at `build_competition`: `raw_by_source.get(source_id, [])` — the source_id for serieb is \"br_football\" with tournament filter \"Serie B\", but `raw_by_source[\"br_football\"]` contains ALL tournaments! I never filter by the `tournament` field in the preference tuples!\n\nFix: filter raw rows by tournament label when the preference entry specifies one. The preference tuples are (source_id, tournament-in-file, display). In build_competition I need to filter rows by `_tournament == tournament` when tournament != \"\".\n\nAlso team counts: serieb/seriec \"272 teams\" = all brf teams. And copadobrasil shows 333 teams / 10566 matches — also wrong (includes all brf rows!). Let me fix: in build_competition, when building season_rows, only include rows whose `tournament` matches the preference's tournament field (empty = all rows from that file).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c5b2550001MZk3fqu5ARy83V","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c5b1758001HVyQ25Eh6y1WGp"}}
