t, look at the counts: br_football 2021 = 491 — the FULL count. Hmm — did the rebucketing produce season=2020 for those rows? Then br_football 2020 would be 264+111=375. Let me check what the 2021 choice shows: br_football: 491 — nope. Let me debug: `_rebucket_season(match_date, season, league)` — season is not None (2021) → `if season is not None: return season`!! THE BUG: I return the passed-in season immediately without applying the Jan-Mar adjustment! The function signature takes season from the date but short-circuits. Fix: apply the Jan-Mar adjustment to the year AFTER: for brf, the input \"season\" is really the calendar year. Restructure: \n\n```python\ndef _rebucket_season(row_date, calendar_year, league):\n    if row_date is None or calendar_year is None: return None\n    if league and row_date.month <= 3: return calendar_year - 1\n    return calendar_year\n```\n\n2. **serieb: 3677** — hmm, earlier count: Serie B rows total = 3677 across 2014-2023 ✓ correct now (275+378+380+381+377+378+302+446+380+380 = 3677 ✓). But wait — with rebucketing, Jan 2021 Serie B rows (67) move to 2020. Serie B 2020 had 302 rows... hmm 302 + 67 = 369?? Serie B 2020 season: 20 teams = 380 matches; brf incomplete (302+Jan2021 67 = 369, still incomplete — fine, data reality). But the CURRENT output shows serieb=3677 total which is right since rebucketing doesn't change totals.\n\nHmm wait — actually why did the total stay 3677 but 2021 didn't get fixed... because the bug #1. After fix, totals stay same.\n\n3. **copadobrasil 2021 → brazilian_cup_matches (92) vs br_football (111)** ✓ — good, the 80% rule picked the dedicated file. But note brf 2021 Copa = 111 — the Feb-Mar 2021 rows (50, 2020-season matches) stay in 2021 since Copa doesn't rebucket. That's why brf count is inflated; the rule handles it ✓.\n\n4. **brasileirao totals**: 8441 matches 2003-2023. Expected: 2003-2005 (552+552+462=1566) + 2006-2021 (380×16=6080) + 2022 (379) + 2023 (377) = 1566+6080+756 = 8402. Actual 8441 — close; 2021 currently 491 (bug #1) instead of 380: 8402 - 380 + 491 = 8513?? Hmm doesn't match. Let me not compute by hand — after fixing bug #1 I'll verify per-season counts: each season 2006-2021 should be ~380, 2003: 552, 2004: 552, 2005: 462, 2022: 379, 2023: 377. Note: with rebucketing, brf 2021 = 380 (491 - 111). And brf 2020 = 264+111 = 375 < bra 380 → bra chosen for 2020 ✓.\n\n5. **copadobrasil 2012 → 112**?? The cup file 2012 = 112 rows... earlier count said copa 2012: 112 ✓ (all scored? 112 rows, were any NA? The 16 NA rows were 2021 only ✓).\n\nLet me fix the rebucket bug now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c5b5d74001JSq2iBePfAsXCo","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c5b3c28001uakwzYFPlNHyQK"}}
