ilian club, not Santos Laguna (Mexico). The substring fallback is too loose here. \n\nBetter approach: club resolution via resolve_team → key \"santos\"; then club_keys = {key} PLUS keys of clubs whose compact EQUALS... hmm. The substring fallback was for cases where the FIFA club name doesn't resolve to a team key (e.g. \"Recife\"?). Actually resolve_team on \"Santos\" gives key \"santos\" ✓ exact — the Brazilian Santos club_key is \"santos\" ✓. FIFA \"Santos\" → club_key \"santos\" ✓ same. FIFA \"Santos Laguna\" → club_key \"santoslaguna\" ≠ \"santos\" — so WITHOUT the substring fallback, \"Santos\" query would return only the Brazilian club ✓ CORRECT. The substring fallback breaks it.\n\nWhy did I add the substring fallback? For clubs like \"Sport Club do Recife\" — resolve_team(\"Sport Club do Recife\") → key \"sportrecife\" ✓ works anyway! The FIFA club names resolve through the same team_key(). So exact key matching suffices. REMOVE the substring fallback — but wait: are there FIFA clubs that DON'T resolve to the same key as their match-file counterparts? I aliased the Brazilian FIFA clubs (sportclubdorecife→sportrecife etc.). What about a query like \"PSG\"? Not a match team — resolve_team fails → AnalysisError \"No team matching 'PSG'\" — hmm, that's bad for player search by non-Brazilian club! E.g. \"Who are the highest-rated players at Paris Saint-Germain?\" → resolve_team(\"Paris Saint-Germain\") → registry has FIFA clubs! \"Paris Saint-Germain\" IS in the registry (from FIFA file names) ✓ resolves to key \"parissaintgermain\" ✓. OK good — the registry includes all FIFA clubs.\n\nBut e.g. \"Man City\"? FIFA says \"Manchester City\" ✓ exact. \"Chelsea\" ✓. So exact key resolution works for FIFA clubs. Remove the substring fallback but keep a safety: if the resolved key has no players AND no substring matches... no — simpler: keep exact key match only. If a user queries a club with slightly different spelling, resolve_team's fuzzy matching handles it.\n\nOne more consideration: resolve_team(\"Santos\") — could fuzzy-pick \"Santos Laguna\" first? Registry find: exact key \"santos\" exists ✓ → exact match wins. ✓.\n\nLet me remove the substring fallback.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c5e3fbd0019mpR1qZlD209sO","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c5e241200169JPXf4WSqjoIY"}}
