{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788256125931,"sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8f272f2d21b0182b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","newString":"# The dedicated Copa do Brasil file numbers rounds inconsistently between\n# seasons (the 2012 final is round 6, the 2016 final round 7, 2013-2020\n# round 8), so finals are detected per season: the highest round of a\n# season played over exactly two legs.\n_LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS = {\n    \"group stage\": \"Group Stage\",\n    \"round of 16\": \"Round of 16\",\n    \"quarterfinals\": \"Quarterfinals\",\n    \"semifinals\": \"Semifinals\",\n    \"final\": \"Final\",\n}\n\n\ndef _stage_label(raw: RawMatch) -> str:\n    if raw.source == \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\" and raw.stage:\n        return _LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS.get(raw.stage.lower(), raw.stage.title())\n    if raw.round_number is not None:\n        return f\"Round {raw.round_number}\"\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef _label_cup_file_finals(matches: list[Match]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Mark two-legged finals in seasons sourced from the dedicated cup file.\"\"\"\n    by_season: dict[int, dict[int, list[Match]]] = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(list))\n    for m in matches:\n        if m.season is not None and m.round_number is not None and m.source != \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\":\n            by_season[m.season][m.round_number].append(m)\n    for season, rounds in by_season.items():\n        max_round = max(rounds)\n        games = rounds[max_round]\n        # A truncated season (e.g. the 2021 file ends at the round of 16)\n        # must not have its last round mislabeled as a final.\n        if len(games) == 2:\n            for m in games:\n                m.stage = \"Final\"","oldString":"# Copa do Brasil (dedicated file) uses round numbers with a fixed structure;\n# round 8 is the final.  The 2021 file is truncated after round 4, so its\n# last round must NOT be mislabeled as a final.\nCUP_ROUND_LABELS = {\n    8: \"Final\",\n    7: \"Semifinal\",\n    6: \"Quarterfinal\",\n    5: \"Round of 16\",\n}\n\n_LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS = {\n    \"group stage\": \"Group Stage\",\n    \"round of 16\": \"Round of 16\",\n    \"quarterfinals\": \"Quarterfinals\",\n    \"semifinals\": \"Semifinals\",\n    \"final\": \"Final\",\n}\n\n\ndef _stage_label(raw: RawMatch) -> str:\n    if raw.source == \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\" and raw.stage:\n        return _LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS.get(raw.stage.lower(), raw.stage.title())\n    if raw.round_number is not None:\n        if raw.source == \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\":\n            return CUP_ROUND_LABELS.get(raw.round_number, f\"Round {raw.round_number}\")\n        return f\"Round {raw.round_number}\"\n    return \"\""},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -417,18 +417,12 @@\n                 partial.append(player)\n         return exact + partial\n \n \n-# Copa do Brasil (dedicated file) uses round numbers with a fixed structure;\n-# round 8 is the final.  The 2021 file is truncated after round 4, so its\n-# last round must NOT be mislabeled as a final.\n-CUP_ROUND_LABELS = {\n-    8: \"Final\",\n-    7: \"Semifinal\",\n-    6: \"Quarterfinal\",\n-    5: \"Round of 16\",\n-}\n-\n+# The dedicated Copa do Brasil file numbers rounds inconsistently between\n+# seasons (the 2012 final is round 6, the 2016 final round 7, 2013-2020\n+# round 8), so finals are detected per season: the highest round of a\n+# season played over exactly two legs.\n _LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS = {\n     \"group stage\": \"Group Stage\",\n     \"round of 16\": \"Round of 16\",\n     \"quarterfinals\": \"Quarterfinals\",\n@@ -440,14 +434,28 @@\n def _stage_label(raw: RawMatch) -> str:\n     if raw.source == \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\" and raw.stage:\n         return _LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS.get(raw.stage.lower(), raw.stage.title())\n     if raw.round_number is not None:\n-        if raw.source == \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\":\n-            return CUP_ROUND_LABELS.get(raw.round_number, f\"Round {raw.round_number}\")\n         return f\"Round {raw.round_number}\"\n     return \"\"\n \n \n+def _label_cup_file_finals(matches: list[Match]) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Mark two-legged finals in seasons sourced from the dedicated cup file.\"\"\"\n+    by_season: dict[int, dict[int, list[Match]]] = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(list))\n+    for m in matches:\n+        if m.season is not None and m.round_number is not None and m.source != \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\":\n+            by_season[m.season][m.round_number].append(m)\n+    for season, rounds in by_season.items():\n+        max_round = max(rounds)\n+        games = rounds[max_round]\n+        # A truncated season (e.g. the 2021 file ends at the round of 16)\n+        # must not have its last round mislabeled as a final.\n+        if len(games) == 2:\n+            for m in games:\n+                m.stage = \"Final\"\n+\n+\n def _label_brf_cup_finals(matches: list[Match]) -> None:\n     \"\"\"Mark final-round matches in BR-Football cup seasons (no round data).\n \n     The final is the two-team pairing played on the last two distinct\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -417,18 +417,12 @@\n                 partial.append(player)\n         return exact + partial\n \n \n-# Copa do Brasil (dedicated file) uses round numbers with a fixed structure;\n-# round 8 is the final.  The 2021 file is truncated after round 4, so its\n-# last round must NOT be mislabeled as a final.\n-CUP_ROUND_LABELS = {\n-    8: \"Final\",\n-    7: \"Semifinal\",\n-    6: \"Quarterfinal\",\n-    5: \"Round of 16\",\n-}\n-\n+# The dedicated Copa do Brasil file numbers rounds inconsistently between\n+# seasons (the 2012 final is round 6, the 2016 final round 7, 2013-2020\n+# round 8), so finals are detected per season: the highest round of a\n+# season played over exactly two legs.\n _LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS = {\n     \"group stage\": \"Group Stage\",\n     \"round of 16\": \"Round of 16\",\n     \"quarterfinals\": \"Quarterfinals\",\n@@ -440,14 +434,28 @@\n def _stage_label(raw: RawMatch) -> str:\n     if raw.source == \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\" and raw.stage:\n         return _LIBERTADORES_STAGE_LABELS.get(raw.stage.lower(), raw.stage.title())\n     if raw.round_number is not None:\n-        if raw.source == \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\":\n-            return CUP_ROUND_LABELS.get(raw.round_number, f\"Round {raw.round_number}\")\n         return f\"Round {raw.round_number}\"\n     return \"\"\n \n \n+def _label_cup_file_finals(matches: list[Match]) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Mark two-legged finals in seasons sourced from the dedicated cup file.\"\"\"\n+    by_season: dict[int, dict[int, list[Match]]] = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(list))\n+    for m in matches:\n+        if m.season is not None and m.round_number is not None and m.source != \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\":\n+            by_season[m.season][m.round_number].append(m)\n+    for season, rounds in by_season.items():\n+        max_round = max(rounds)\n+        games = rounds[max_round]\n+        # A truncated season (e.g. the 2021 file ends at the round of 16)\n+        # must not have its last round mislabeled as a final.\n+        if len(games) == 2:\n+            for m in games:\n+                m.stage = \"Final\"\n+\n+\n def _label_brf_cup_finals(matches: list[Match]) -> None:\n     \"\"\"Mark final-round matches in BR-Football cup seasons (no round data).\n \n     The final is the two-team pairing played on the last two distinct\n","additions":20,"deletions":12},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/loader.py","time":{"start":1788256125928,"end":1788256125930}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting — the Copa file's round numbers are inconsistent between seasons:\n- 2012: rounds 1-6, with round 6 = 2 matches (the FINAL! Palmeiras vs Coritiba 2 legs). So 2012's final is round 6, not 8!\n- 2013: rounds 1-8, round 8 = 2 (final)\n- 2016: rounds 1-7, round 7 = 2 (final!)\n- 2017: rounds 1-8, round 8 = 2 (final)\n\nSo the round numbering varies by season (2012: 6 rounds total; 2013-2015: 8; 2016: 7; 2017-2020: 8). My hardcoded CUP_ROUND_LABELS {8: Final, 7: Semifinal...} is WRONG for 2012 and 2016!\n\n- 2012: final = round 6 → my labels: round 6 = \"Quarterfinal\" ✗ and no \"Final\" → 2012 final missing from competition_finals ✗ (explains why 2012 was missing!)\n- 2016: final = round 7 → labeled \"Semifinal\" ✗ and round 6 (semifinal) labeled \"Quarterfinal\" ✗\n\nFIX: determine the final round per season dynamically: the final = the round with exactly 2 matches at the END of the season... Actually more robust: for each season, the FINAL round = the max round number that has ≤ 2 matches and all rounds after it have ≤ 2 matches... Hmm.\n\nSimplest robust rule for this file: within each season, the final is the LAST round (max round number) when the max round has exactly 2 matches (2 legs) — 2012: max round 6 with 2 ✓; 2013: max 8 with 2 ✓; 2016: max 7 with 2 ✓; 2017-2020: max 8 with 2 ✓; 2021: max 4 with 16 matches ✗ (not 2 → no final ✓ correct since file truncated!).\n\nWait 2021: rounds {1:40, 2:20, 3:32, 4:16} — max round 4 has 16 matches ≠ 2 → correctly NO final ✓.\n\nSo rule: per season, final matches = matches in max round IF that round has exactly 2 matches. Semifinal = second-max round if it has ≤ 4 matches? 2012: rounds 1-6, round 5 = 4 matches (semis ✓). 2016: round 6 = 4 (semis ✓). 2013: round 7 = 4 ✓. General: label rounds generically as \"Round N\" except the final; and semifinal if the round has exactly 4 matches and is the second-highest round. Let me keep it simpler and safer:\n- Final: max round with exactly 2 matches in that season → stage \"Final\"\n- Everything else: \"Round N\"\n\nAlso drop the CUP_ROUND_LABELS dict. For brf-sourced seasons, the last-pairing heuristic stays (verified 2022/2023 work).\n\nBut wait — there's also the case where a season's max round has >2 matches due to truncation (2021) → no Final ✓.\n\nHmm, one more check — 2016: rounds {1:75, 2:37, 3:20, 4:16, 5:8, 6:4, 7:2} — max round 7 = 2 ✓ final. And the semis (round 6, 4 matches) ✓ labeled \"Round 6\" — fine.\n\nAlso 2014: earlier showed rounds for 2014? Not printed, but pattern 2013/2015 similar (1:2?? weird \"round 1: 2 matches\" for 2013 — the file has odd leftovers; fine).\n\nLet me fix `_stage_label` to not hardcode, and compute finals in `_label_cup_finals`-style post-processing over ALL cup sources:\n\nNew plan for stage labeling:\n1. Initial pass: stage = \"Round N\" (cup file + leagues), Libertadores stage mapping (unchanged).\n2. Post-pass for Copa do Brasil (all sources):\n   - For seasons from the cup file: final = max-round matches if count == 2 → \"Final\".\n   - For brf seasons: last-pairing heuristic (existing `_label_brf_cup_finals`).\n\nImplementation: replace `_stage_label`'s CUP_ROUND_LABELS with generic \"Round N\", and add `_label_cup_file_finals(matches)` that groups by season, finds max round, checks count == 2, labels them \"Final\". Then in build_competition for copadobrasil: run both `_label_cup_file_finals` and `_label_brf_cup_finals`.\n\nLet me apply this fix.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c5ef83e001baneZbC4oXl293","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c5ed494001FrviBn6ynylEoI"}}
