{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788256144172,"sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9f83e651177ed855","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nimport server\nsrv = server.build_server()\n\nasync def call(tool, args):\n    res = await srv.call_tool(tool, args)\n    return res.content[0].text\n\n# separate event loops, like pytest-bdd steps will do\nt1 = asyncio.run(call(\"search_matches\", {\"team\": \"Flamengo\", \"limit\": 1}))\nt2 = asyncio.run(call(\"champion\", {\"competition\": \"Brasileirão\", \"season\": 2019}))\nt3 = asyncio.run(call(\"list_competitions\", {}))\nprint(t1.splitlines()[0])\nprint(t2.splitlines()[0])\nprint(\"OK - separate loops work\")\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-9b01b8399d96"},"output":"Flamengo (958 matches in dataset):\n2019 Brasileirão Serie A champion: Flamengo\nOK - separate loops work\n","metadata":{"output":"Flamengo (958 matches in dataset):\n2019 Brasileirão Serie A champion: Flamengo\nOK - separate loops work\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nimport server\nsrv = server.build_server()\n\nasync def call(tool, args):\n    res = await srv.call_tool(tool, args)\n    return res.content[0].text\n\n# separate event loops, like pytest-bdd steps will do\nt1 = asyncio.run(call(\"search_matches\", {\"team\": \"Flamengo\", \"limit\": 1}))\nt2 = asyncio.run(call(\"champion\", {\"competition\": \"Brasileirão\", \"season\": 2019}))\nt3 = asyncio.run(call(\"list_competitions\", {}))\nprint(t1.splitlines()[0])\nprint(t2.splitlines()[0])\nprint(\"OK - separate loops work\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788256144108,"end":1788256144170}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the Copa finals list is complete and correct:\n- 2012 Palmeiras ✓ (real!), 2013 Flamengo ✓, 2014 Atlético-MG ✓, 2015 pens-tie ✓ (real: Palmeiras on pens), 2016 Grêmio ✓, 2017 pens-tie ✓ (real: Cruzeiro on pens), 2018 Cruzeiro ✓, 2019 Athletico ✓, 2020 Palmeiras ✓, 2022 pens-tie ✓ (Flamengo on pens), 2023 São Paulo ✓\n\nAll match reality. Now write the full BDD test suite. Let me create:\n\n1. `tests/conftest.py` — fixtures + shared BDD steps\n2. `tests/features/*.feature` — 8 feature files\n3. `tests/test_*.py` — step definitions\n4. `pytest.ini`, `requirements.txt`\n\nLet me write them all now. Design shared steps in conftest to be reusable across features:\n\nconftest.py:\n- session fixtures: soccer_data, mcp_server\n- `ctx` fresh dict per scenario\n- shared given steps: \"the match data is loaded\", \"the player data is loaded\", \"the MCP server is running\"\n- shared when: generic tool call with args mini-DSL: When I call the tool \"X\" with arguments \"k=v, k=v\"\n- shared then: response contains \"...\"\n\nFor feature steps local to each module, define in test files.\n\npytest-bdd 8.1: `from pytest_bdd import scenarios, given, when, then, parsers`. `scenarios(\"features/xxx.feature\")` — path relative to the test file.\n\nOne critical detail: pytest-bdd scenarios are collected from the .feature file, and steps are resolved from fixtures in the test module AND conftest.py ✓.\n\nasyncio: steps call `asyncio.run(...)` — note that asyncio.run creates a new loop; the MCPServer instance — is it loop-bound? MCPServer.call_tool creates streams? It should work per-call with fresh loops... hmm, potential issue: anyio primitives bound to a loop. Earlier smoke tests called asyncio.run(main()) once with MULTIPLE call_tool invocations inside ONE loop. If each STEP does asyncio.run(call_tool(...)) separately — each call in a fresh loop. Does MCPServer.call_tool carry cross-loop state? The tool functions are sync (run in thread executor). call_tool is async — probably fine with fresh loops. Let me just verify quickly with two sequential asyncio.run calls before writing everything.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c5f410c001fkKfAyVW2rzLI6","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","messageID":"msg_05c5f2aa7001XT6jDDdJh7amDg"}}
