{"type":"text","timestamp":1788256440923,"sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","part":{"id":"prt_05c63c9c6001QS7OjBYK844Kvc","messageID":"msg_05c63c0250013OiARqi2g0LM8B","sessionID":"ses_fa3ba9cb2ffeFGH9rzdcVMfYFE","type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. **64/64 tests pass**, all spec requirements met.\n\n## What was built\n\n**`server.py`** — MCP server (stdio + streamable-http) exposing **18 tools** + a dataset resource, covering all five required capability categories: match queries, team queries, player queries, competition queries, and statistical analysis.\n\n**`brazilian_soccer/`** — the knowledge base:\n- **`normalize.py`** — folds 1,150 raw team-name variants (`Palmeiras-SP`, `Sport Club Corinthians Paulista`, `Athletico`, `Nacional (URU)`…) into canonical keys, with namesake protection (`Flamengo - PI` ≠ Flamengo)\n- **`loader.py`** — unifies the 6 CSVs: one source per competition-season (80% coverage rule), COVID season re-bucketing (BR-Football's Jan–Mar rows belong to the previous season), skips unplayable rows, and enriches matches with corners/shots/stadiums via cross-file joins\n- **`analysis.py` / `formatting.py`** — queries + spec-style answer rendering\n\n## Key validation points (verified against real-world facts)\n\n- 2019 Brasileirão table computed exactly: Flamengo champion, 90 pts, correct relegation zones for 2018/2020/2023\n- Copa do Brasil finals detected correctly despite inconsistent round numbering per season — every winner from 2012–2023 matches history\n- Libertadores finals with penalty-shootout notes for level aggregates (2013, 2015, 2017, 2022)\n\n## Tests\n\n8 Gherkin feature files (pytest-bdd) mirroring the spec's BDD scenarios + unit tests + a real stdio end-to-end test that spawns `server.py` and drives it through an MCP `ClientSession`. Performance criteria (<2s lookups, <5s aggregates) asserted explicitly. README documents 25 answerable sample questions, all data decisions, and known limitations.","time":{"start":1788256438726,"end":1788256440914}}}
